/-!
# The conditional forward continuation in MS93 (4.3.2)

The backward commutator bound gives Z_start <= Vcirc_back Z_back for each
actual backward choice. Residual spans for selected configurations give the
normal forward product on the original critical path. The latter argument
transports the entire selection and retains the incident edge and its escape
from the transported far kernel.

These are conditional helpers for the continuation assembly. This module
does not construct the backward bounds or the residual spans.
Source: Meierfrankenfeld--Stellmacher (1993), printed pp.885--886.
-/
